ttps://github.com/lnreader/lnreader/releases/download/v2.1.4/SHA256SUMS.txt"}], "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/lnreader/lnreader/tarball/v2.1.4", "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/lnreader/lnreader/zipball/v2.1.4", "body": "\r\nThis release adds shared-link support, crash reporting, and more control over categories and background tasks, along with safer backup restores and a round of stability fixes.\r\n\r\n### New features\r\n\r\n- Open a novel directly, or search for it, by sharing its URL to LNReader.\r\n- Find crash logs and diagnostic details in Advanced settings to help troubleshoot issues.\r\n- Set category selection to \"Always ask\" to choose categories each time you add a novel to your library.\r\n- Show optional continue reading buttons on novel covers and list items in the library.\r\n- Cancel any queued or running background task individually from the task queue.\r\n\r\n### Improvements\r\n\r\n- Refined the custom code editor, snippet controls, genre taxonomy screen, and statistics layout.\r\n- Reduced background task memory usage and improved task lifecycle management.\r\n- Backup restores are now non-destructive and preserve existing data where appropriate.\r\n- Updated translations.\r\n\r\n### Fixes\r\n\r\n- Fixed crashes when chapter or novel names are missing.\r\n- Fixed blank or empty-state flashes when opening the chapter drawer and novel screen.\r\n- Fixed bottom navigation icons shifting when switching tabs.\r\n- Fixed text-to-speech handling of dash-only dividers and surrounding quotation marks.\r\n- Fixed newline handling in the code editor and restored the broken preview.", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/lnreader/lnreader/releases/397143726/reactions", "total_count": 12, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 6, "confused": 0, "heart": 6, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}}}